ield/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e33a131a-3563-58bc-8125-e3be42bd649b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377445} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac570af-b695-5d99-96db-859f505d5ee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377446} {:answer/id #uuid "ccae325a-4edd-55e8-94f4-567327cee256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e33a131a-3563-58bc-8125-e3be42bd649b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377445} :answer-field/id #uuid "73c4f8cd-27ec-5bc9-93d4-edba7df1d63d" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99eec602-804d-52f4-910f-ce3400861096" :question/math-academy-id "q-333034" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072827/assets/f20c6478af528b45ab2ea7dfded3e835c49a79178e11d7dd06bb13760874bbdb.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above.\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }3]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}." :question/worked-solution "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-3x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072827/assets/ed058963b391a4cdc66b2ab48483906a4d07759681c1f24e47ffc9e10775895f.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}<0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072827/assets/6c92028370c86431ddc6ccd9513c273054d98b5add159e1bddf5a2e11751d987.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{away from the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ada3a84a-f979-5aee-9422-7acb8e430c11" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Phase Portrait of a System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b074167-c621-5939-a802-ed9580a22aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377450} {:answer/id #uuid "8d11edae-ad17-5da0-aa94-1464d0aad159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377451} {:answer/id #uuid "c7522b34-3cc2-50d9-ac72-3028e9fba9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377452} {:answer/id #uuid "9e04d3f3-a1bf-560b-9474-e660de673faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d11edae-ad17-5da0-aa94-1464d0aad159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377451} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad643d0-ce29-5074-b9dc-7fbbd4961a5e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377449} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d51bd7-251e-55b4-af66-cf1f59c702dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377455} {:answer/id #uuid "88c117fe-6ee0-5ab9-b3c9-8e0b6eafcbcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15d51bd7-251e-55b4-af66-cf1f59c702dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377455} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bdb2563-b271-5b0b-a942-cb54e0607b74" :answer-field/key "field-10" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377454} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0